            <section ID="id_link_513d4e05-96e5-7f6b-e063-6294a90a4edd">
               <id root="5143155b-32bc-b67c-e063-6294a90adda0"/>
               <code code="34089-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="DESCRIPTION SECTION"/>
               <title>
                  <content styleCode="bold">DESCRIPTION:</content>
               </title>
               <text>
                  <paragraph>
                     <content styleCode="bold">Digenyx™</content> (Hyoscyamine Sulfate USP, 0.125 mg) tablets are off-white to light beige round tablet containing 0.125 mg hyoscyamine sulfate formulated for oral administration. Each tablet also contains inactive ingredients: Lactose Monohydrate, Magnesium Stearate, Microcrystalline Cellulose, Stearic Acid, Sodium Starch Glycolate.
  <br/>
                     <br/>
Hyoscyamine sulfate is one of the principal anticholinergic/antispasmodic components of belladonna alkaloids. The empirical formula is (C
  <sub>17</sub>H
  <sub>23</sub>NO
  <sub>3</sub>)
  <sub>2</sub>• H
  <sub>2</sub>SO
  <sub>4</sub>• 2H
  <sub>2</sub>O and the molecular weight is 712.85. Chemically, it is benzeneacetic acid,α-(hydroxymethyl)-, 8-methyl-8-azabicyclo [3.2.1] oct-3-yl ester, [3(S)-endo]-, sulfate (2:1), dihydrate with the following structure:
 </paragraph>
                  <paragraph/>
                  <paragraph>
                     <renderMultiMedia referencedObject="img_513d5669-325b-5b20-e063-6294a90ac988"/>
                  </paragraph>
               </text>
               <effectiveTime value="20260507"/>
